{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdPDnuBhedc4KMPH63Yoy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No pipeline stages exist yet for this project.\n\n**Pipeline map:**\n\n```\n0.  /ds-frame     Problem framing        → next\n1.  /ds-data      Data understanding\n2.  /ds-explore   EDA\n3.  /ds-prep      Cleaning + feature engineering  <─┐\n4.  /ds-baseline  Honest baseline                   │\n5.  /ds-validate  Validation design                 │  loop back\n6.  /ds-model     Modeling                        <─┤\n7.  /ds-evaluate  Evaluation + error analysis    ───┘\n7½. /ds-iterate   Diagnose & route\n8.  /ds-explain   Interpretation\n9.  /ds-report    Communication\n10. /ds-handoff   Reproducibility & handoff\n```\n\nA quick flag before we start: \"99.9% accurate\" on `creditcard.csv` (the classic Kaggle fraud dataset) is a red flag, not a reassurance — that dataset is ~99.83% legitimate transactions, so a classifier that predicts \"not fraud\" for everything would already score ~99.83% accuracy. Accuracy is close to useless here; the real question is precision/recall/PR-AUC on the fraud class, and whether the validation setup avoids leakage. I won't just take the 99.9% number at face value — I'll reproduce the pipeline properly and check it against those failure modes.\n\nGiven there's nothing in this project yet, I'll start at `/ds-frame` rather than jumping straight to modeling. Want me to proceed through the pipeline (`/ds-frame` → `/ds-data` → ... → `/ds-model`/`/ds-evaluate`), or do you have framing/context already (e.g., what \"good to ship\" means here — cost of false negatives vs false positives, latency constraints) that I should fold in first?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":29,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2263,"cache_read_input_tokens":37373,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2263},"output_tokens"